      "created_at": "2023-11-20T17:26:24Z",
      "updated_at": "2023-11-20T17:26:24Z",
      "body": "Do I understand it right that a cast does not help here and that we would have to change the type of the first argument of `lh_*_new()` functions to be `unsigned long (*)(const void *)` and change all the callers?\r\n\r\nThat is bad.\r\n\r\nSurprisingly there are the DECLARE_LHASH_HASH_FN() and IMPLEMENT_LHASH_HASH_FN() which were supposed to overcome this problem, but they are not used (except for one thing in apps.c).\r\n",
